{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>ויסר.</b> From the heavy doubled binyan, and it should have been ויסר with a small patach under the samekh, and I have already mentioned its grammar." "And some say that the meaning of ויסר את אפן מרכבותיו is that he loosened the binding of the wheel from the horses, to flee because they were swift, and the confusion of HaShem written above fell upon them and upon their horses, and they could not drive them except with difficulty. And others said that it is from the root of סורר (Deuteronomy 21:18), that the one going before them intended to turn the chariot aside." "<b>נלחם להם במצרים.</b> On their behalf. And the word of HaShem was fulfilled, which He said, וידעו מצרים כי אני ה' (above, chapter 4), before their death."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:34:30.155026554Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}